Where Does AccessDeniedHandler Fit?

A request passes through Spring Security like this:

                 HTTP Request
                      │
                      ▼
           JwtAuthenticationFilter
                      │
                      ▼
          SecurityContextHolder
                      │
                      ▼
           Authorization Manager
                      │
        ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐
        ▼                           ▼
   Has Permission?                No Permission
        │                           │
        ▼                           ▼
   Controller              AccessDeniedHandler
                                    │
                                    ▼
                            403 Forbidden

Notice the difference:

AuthenticationEntryPoint → User is not authenticated.
AccessDeniedHandler → User is authenticated, but not authorized.








